{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short --branch && git log --oneline --decorate -12 && gh pr view 35 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,isDraft,baseRefName,headRefName,mergeable,reviewDecision,body,commits,files,comments,reviews'","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"body\":\"Closes #33\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #33 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-19T18:53:02Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-19T18:53:02Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Replaces `vgt read-chords`/`vgt_read_chords.lua` and\\n`vgt read-sections`/`vgt_read_sections.lua` with a single `vgt sync` /\\n`vgt_sync.lua` action that reads both the [vgt] Chords track's items and\\n[vgt]-owned section regions back into the sidecar as human-verified, in\\none invocation.\\n\\nAlso extends #19's detected/value split (previously chords-only) to the\\nsections stage (sidecar schema v4 -> v5, migrated with the same\\nbest-effort backfill used for chords' v2 -> v3), so a human correction to\\nsections never destroys the original machine-detected boundaries -- the\\ndata model `vgt sync` needs to keep both versions available for both\\nstages, per #33's dependency on #19's follow-up.\\n\\nCloses #33.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat: consolidate chord + section read-back into one `vgt sync` command\",\"oid\":\"566fb9f7b29e0cd5b9c54d0a2820b81805efd5ac\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"additions\":32,\"deletions\":30,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"docs/GOAL.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":3,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"reascript/vgt_initialize.lua\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"reascript/vgt_read_sections.lua\",\"additions\":0,\"deletions\":230,\"changeType\":\"DELETED\"},{\"path\":\"reascript/vgt_sync.lua\",\"additions\":129,\"deletions\":62,\"changeType\":\"RENAMED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/analysis.py\",\"additions\":32,\"deletions\":9,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/cli.py\",\"additions\":11,\"deletions\":17,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/sidecar.py\",\"additions\":22,\"deletions\":12,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/status.py\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_analysis.py\",\"additions\":57,\"deletions\":6,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_project.py\",\"additions\":3,\"deletions\":10,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_reascript.py\",\"additions\":68,\"deletions\":114,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefName\":\"issue-33-consolidate-chord-section-read-back-into\",\"isDraft\":false,\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"number\":35,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Consolidate chord + section read-back into one 'sync' (synchronize) command\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
