tected`\ntests/test_analysis.py:428:    assert chords[\"detected_input_hash\"]  # sanity: the refresh path did run\ntests/test_analysis.py:447:        \"human_verified\": True,\ntests/test_analysis.py:456:    assert result[\"analysis\"][\"sections\"][\"human_verified\"] is True\ntests/test_analysis.py:460:def test_sync_style_correction_preserves_original_detected_sections(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\ntests/test_analysis.py:461:    \"\"\"Mirrors what `vgt_sync.lua` does for sections: overwrite only `value`\ntests/test_analysis.py:462:    and set `human_verified`, leaving `detected` untouched -- the same #19\ntests/test_analysis.py:463:    guarantee `test_analyze_style_chord_correction_preserves_original_detected`\ntests/test_analysis.py:469:    original_detected = first[\"analysis\"][\"sections\"][\"detected\"]\ntests/test_analysis.py:470:    assert original_detected == first[\"analysis\"][\"sections\"][\"value\"]\ntests/test_analysis.py:475:    sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"sections\"][\"human_verified\"] = True\ntests/test_analysis.py:482:    assert sections[\"human_verified\"] is True\ntests/test_analysis.py:483:    assert sections[\"detected\"] == original_detected\ntests/test_analysis.py:484:    assert sections[\"detected\"] != corrected_sections\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:22:    sync = subparsers.add_parser(\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:23:        \"sync\",\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:29:    sync.add_argument(\"project\", nargs=\"?\", help=\"Path to a .RPP project (defaults to cwd's only .RPP).\")\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:49:    if not arguments or arguments[0] not in {\"inspect\", \"apply\", \"sync\", \"analyze\", \"status\", \"-h\", \"--help\"}:\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:73:            \"sync\": (\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:74:                \"vgt_sync.lua\",\nREADME.md:50:`human_verified: true`; `vgt analyze` then leaves that stage untouched on\nREADME.md:52:Each detected stage records its UTC `analyzed_at` time; a correction records\nREADME.md:65:  the optional `madmom` extra (`uv sync --extra madmom`). madmom's last\nREADME.md:72:  setting (or `4/4`) rather than a detected bar length.\nREADME.md:75:next to the sidecar — a bare click on the detected beat grid (the reference\nREADME.md:79:The tempo stage's `value` also stores the raw detected `beat_times` — the\nREADME.md:80:shared beat-synchronous grid the `chords` stage below aligns to.\nREADME.md:95:(not a separately detected grid):\nREADME.md:117:`detected` (the pristine machine detection, untouched by corrections). With\nREADME.md:119:for good, but `detected` keeps tracking the current reference audio and\nREADME.md:121:it stays live even while the human's `value` is frozen. Refreshing `detected`\nREADME.md:135:  the optional `msaf` extra (`uv sync --extra msaf`). Like madmom above,\nREADME.md:148:`human_verified: true` is set. Every run also renders a **section-timeline\nREADME.md:150:detected structure can be checked by eye; it is vgt-owned and regenerated\nREADME.md:157:carry the detected beat-aligned labels. Unlike every other vgt-owned label\nREADME.md:163:the action writes the detected tempo map. If the project already has any other\nREADME.md:182:Auto-detected chords and sections are sometimes wrong, and correcting raw\nREADME.md:184:in REAPER, then run one action — `vgt sync` — to read every manual edit back\nREADME.md:196:**Sections**: rename or move the `[vgt]` regions vgt created for detected\nREADME.md:200:[reascript/vgt_sync.lua](reascript/vgt_sync.lua) in REAPER's Action List and\nREADME.md:201:run it (or run `vgt sync [project.rpp]` for the same pointer from the CLI).\nREADME.md:207:  `analysis.chords.value.segments` with `chords.human_verified: true`;\nREADME.md:211:  `sections.human_verified: true`;\nREADME.md:212:- never touches `analysis.chords.detected` or `analysis.sections.detected` —\nREADME.md:226:particular, the `chords` line says whether it is only machine-detected or\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:11:       gains a `detected` sibling of `value` holding the pristine\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:12:       machine-detected chords, so a human correction to `value` never\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:14:       migrated by backfilling `detected` from `value` (best effort -- if a\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:16:       gone and the backfill just seeds `detected` with the corrected chords).\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:20:  5 -- The `sections` stage gains the same `detected`/`value` split as\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:21:       `chords` (#19's follow-up, consumed by `vgt sync`, see #33): a human\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:22:       correction to `value` never destroys the original detected section\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:24:       chords were: `detected` is backfilled from `value` (best effort).\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:29:    \"human_verified\": bool,   # true once a human has corrected/confirmed it\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:32:    \"analyzed_at\": str | null, # UTC time at which this value was detected\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:35:A human correction is applied by setting \"value\" and \"human_verified\": true;\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:41:    \"detected\": <machine-detected value, independent of human corrections>,\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:42:    \"detected_input_hash\": str | null,    # hash `detected` was last computed against\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:43:    \"detected_settings_hash\": str | null,\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:45:`detected` is never touched by `vgt sync`; only `vgt analyze`'s detectors\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:46:write it. Unlike `value`, `detected` keeps tracking the current audio and\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:49:`value` is what freezes (see `analysis.py`'s `_refresh_stage_with_detected`).\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:68:# Stages that carry the detected/value split (#19): a human correction to\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:69:# `value` never overwrites the pristine machine detection kept in `detected`.\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:85:        \"human_verified\": False,\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:93:def _empty_detected_split_stage() -> dict[str, Any]:\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:94:    return {**_empty_stage(), \"detected\": None, \"detected_input_hash\": None, \"detected_settings_hash\": None}\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:117:            merged = {**_empty_detected_split_stage(), **(analysis.get(stage) or {})}\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:118:            if merged[\"detected\"] is None and merged[\"value\"] is not None:\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:120:                # chords, v4 -> v5 for sections). Assume `detected` was last\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:123:                merged[\"detected\"] = copy.deepcopy(merged[\"value\"])\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:124:                merged[\"detected_input_hash\"] = merged[\"input_hash\"]\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:125:                merged[\"detected_settings_hash\"] = merged[\"settings_hash\"]\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:143:    if stage.get(\"human_verified\"):\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:162:    if stage.get(\"human_verified\"):\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:168:        \"human_verified\": False,\ntests/test_status.py:39:            \"chords\": {\"value\": {\"segments\": [{}, {}], \"chord_sheet_path\": f\"{project.stem}.vgt-chords.txt\"}, \"detected\": {\"segments\": [{}, {}, {}]}, \"human_verified\": True, \"analyzed_at\": \"2026-07-19T10:00:00Z\", \"verified_at\": \"2026-07-19T11:00:00Z\"},\ntests/test_status.py:45:    assert \"120.0 BPM, 4/4, detected\" in text\ntests/test_status.py:46:    assert \"A# minor, detected\" in text\ntests/test_status.py:47:    assert \"2 sections, detected\" in text\ntests/test_status.py:48:    assert \"2 segments, human-corrected, detected baseline present\" in text\ntests/test_status.py:55:    assert status[\"stages\"][\"chords\"][\"detected_present\"] is True\nsrc/vgt/tempo.py:78:        raise TempoDetectionError(f\"Too few beats detected in {source} to build a tempo grid.\")\nsrc/vgt/tempo.py:190:    \"\"\"Render a click-only track on the detected beat grid so it can be checked\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:12:`analysis` and snap chord boundaries to it -- the shared beat-synchronous\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:60:    raw detected beat times (see tempo.py) -- the last of these is the shared\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:96:    only refreshing the `detected` baseline of an already human-verified\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:97:    stage (see `_refresh_stage_with_detected`), so the on-disk\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:111:def _refresh_stage_with_detected(\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:120:    \"\"\"Like `sidecar.refresh_stage`, but tracks `detected` -- the pristine\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:125:    is only one detector call; `detected` is just the pristine copy of its\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:129:    but `detected` keeps tracking the current audio/settings via its own\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:130:    `detected_input_hash`/`detected_settings_hash` pair, recomputing whenever\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:131:    those change (or `force`). `value` and `human_verified` are never touched\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:132:    by that recompute; only `detected` moves, preserving the human's\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:134:    if not stage.get(\"human_verified\"):\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:142:            \"detected\": copy.deepcopy(refreshed[\"value\"]),\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:143:            \"detected_input_hash\": input_hash,\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:144:            \"detected_settings_hash\": settings_hash,\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:147:    detected_is_current = (\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:148:        stage.get(\"detected_input_hash\") == input_hash and stage.get(\"detected_settings_hash\") == settings_hash\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:150:    if not force and detected_is_current:\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:154:        \"detected\": compute(render_artifact=False),\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:155:        \"detected_input_hash\": input_hash,\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:156:        \"detected_settings_hash\": settings_hash,\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:164:    array) re-detected fresh via the same primary/fallback ladder tempo.py\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:189:    only refreshing the `detected` baseline of an already human-verified\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:190:    stage (see `_refresh_stage_with_detected`), so the on-disk `.vgt-chords.txt` --\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:231:    and stages marked `human_verified` are never recomputed.\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:264:        if analysis[stage].get(\"human_verified\"):\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:267:                or analysis[stage].get(\"detected_input_hash\") != input_hash\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:268:                or analysis[stage].get(\"detected_settings_hash\") != settings_hash\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:270:                emit(f\"[{position}/{total}] {stage} — human-verified value kept; refreshing detected baseline…\")\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:279:        refresh = _refresh_stage_with_detected if stage in DETECTED_SPLIT_STAGES else refresh_stage\nsrc/vgt/sections.py:223:    section) for by-eye verification of the detected structure.\"\"\"\ntests/test_chords.py:82:    grid passed in (not some independently detected one).\"\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
